## Original Content
The support will benefit children in three Sudanese states; West Darfur, South Kordofan and Gedaref with the aim of restoring “safe, quality and inclusive education” amid the world's largest humanitarian and displacement crisis.

## Summary
The United Nations has launched a $22 million education initiative to support children in Sudan's West Darfur, South Kordofan, and Gedaref states. This program aims to restore safe, quality, and inclusive education amidst one of the world's largest humanitarian and displacement crises.

## Key Points
- UN invests $22 million in an education program for Sudanese children.
- Initiative targets three specific states: West Darfur, South Kordofan, and Gedaref.
- Goal is to restore education in areas affected by conflict and displacement.
- Context highlights Sudan's severe humanitarian crisis as a backdrop.


